==Tips & Tricks==
* When farming [[Mastery|mastery]] with Gravity, the user can aim the held version of {{Ability|C}} under a tree to not only place the move closer to the ground, but also pull more enemies to it. This can also help the user attack NPCs while stunned in the attack to deal extra damage with {{Ability|V}} and {{Ability|Z}}.
* Starlight Gravity's {{Ability|X}} changes the way it looks, giving the fly debris a yellowish trail, unlike the normal variant which give no trail.
* The user can dash forward while using the normal version of {{Ability|C}} to combo extend with decently ranged moves like [[Sanguine Art]]'s {{Ability|Sanguine Art|C}}.
* Using {{Ability|X}} is great for damaging enemies to group them up.
* The player can simply use {{Ability|F}}'s held variant to fly just high enough so mobs cannot hit the player, while the player's skills work with no problem.
* For the 1st and 2nd upgrade quest, it is recommended to kill the NPCs in the [[First Sea], as they are highly under-leveled and easy to kill.
* For the third upgrade via the [[Admin Panel]], it is recommended to ask a player, friend or person to spawn their boat. The player can then damage the boat using Gravity's skills. Players should note that their friend has to be on the opposite team or is not allied.
* The user can camp near or on water by dragging players into the water using the normal version of {{Ability|C}} dealing large damage and can easily one-shot the opponent.
* For the 4th upgrade quest '''(Part 2)''' via the [[Admin Panel]], It is recommended going to the [[First Sea]] to kill low-level players. Since '''progress''' counts regardless of the level of the player killed, it makes the quest much easier to complete overall.
* There is currently a bug wherein if the player holds Gravity '''[F] Shooting Star''' in the air, they ride with a layout block instead of the default boulder.
* When the player uses '''[F]''' Shooting Star when they are drowning, the boulder is black instead of the default boulder. This proves that the ground in the [[Water|Sea]] is black.

