==Trivia==
* Gravity is the cheapest {{Mythical}} [[fruit]] in the game.
* The second rework concept of the Gravity moves was created by concept artist @crazy_rtx.
* Gravity and [[Control]] are the only fruits to have different m1 variants, both having 3.
* As of now, Gravity is the only fruit with 20 abilities, making it the fruit with the highest number of skills in the game (including [M1] clicks and their stages).
* The boss [[Orbitus]] uses two moves, in which are similar to the old Gravity Z (Gravity Push) and the old Gravity V (Meteor Rain) the only exception being that the visuals and audio are reworked.
* Gravity is one of the first two fruits that could obtain upgrades through the [[Admin Panel]], the other being [[Eagle]], the second is [[Lightning]], the third is [[Pain]], the fourth is [[Control]], and soon, possibly, [[Creation]].
* Gravity is one of eight fruits to have a [[Power Meter|meter]] that is not intended for a transformation (along with [[Eagle]], [[Creation]], [[Sound]], [[Pain]], [[Shadow]], [[Spirit]] and [[Control]]).
* Gravity is one of fruits that require the most tasks and items to fully upgrade it through the [[Admin Panel]].
* Gravity is the first fruit to feature a cutscene with its held {{Ability|V}}, followed by [[Tiger]] and its [[Werewolf]] mutation, with the held {{Ability|Tiger|C}} and {{Ability|Tiger|F}} respectively, the third being [[Control]]'s {{Ability|Control|V}}, and the fourth being [[Empyrean]] transformed {{Ability|Empyrean|C}}.
* Gravity currently has the longest cutscene of any fruit, being roughly 13.79 seconds.
* Gravity has been reworked two times and has two moves that are uncancellable.
* When going through doorways while flying, the boulder will purposely lower into the ground to allow the user to enter.
* {{Ability|C}}'s upgraded version is very similar to an [[Admin Abilities|admin ability]] called "Tensei".
* Removing the stage 2 [M1] upgrade does not shorten the time to reach stage 3. However, removing the stage 1 [M1] causes the stage 3 animation to play for a short time before becoming normal.
* A physical Gravity fruit can be dropped from defeating the [[Tyrant of the Skies]], at a very low chance.
* Gravity, [[Blade]] and [[Bomb]] are the only fruits that have had their entire moveset reworked twice.
* Gravity's {{Ability|TAP}} has an alternative button on mobile located above {{Ability|Z}} that functions just the same as tapping, although resembles the activation of a move instead.
* Unlike other M1 attacks on mobile, 2 taps are required to activate the {{Ability|TAP}} ability, similar to [[Creation]] and [[Lightning]]
* Gravity and [[Tiger]] are the only fruits to have a cutscene that affect's both parties screens with the same cutscene.
* Before [[Updates/26|Update 26]], Gravity was called to be one of the lamest mythical fruits in the whole game. It was also one of the lowest demanded fruits in the whole Blox Fruits community.
* Gravity's {{Ability|V}} has one of the largest hitboxes in the game.
* While performing the held {{Ability|V}}, the sky turns to [[Full Moon]] night, resetting to day after the attack, regardless of time. It heavily disrupts the cycles.
* Gravity was the first {{Mythical}} fruit to receive upgrades via the [[Admin Panel]], with [[Control]] being the second in [[Updates/29.0|Update 29]].
* Gravity has the longest [M1] range in the game.

